WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:05.600
So often we march like robots through our
broken educational system.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.679
And if we continue like this, we may one day
have a robot as the President of the United

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:12.679
States.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.389
Oh, you don't think it's possible?

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:15.889
Here's what his campaign would sound like.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:22.560
[robotic voice] "I am R-Gen 1 and I am running
for President of the United States of America.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.570
I am the most qualified candidate because
unlike humans, I have no emotions.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:32.800
I make decisions based on pure logic, because
I have the most powerful processor in the

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:33.800
world.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.489
I won't just make America great again.

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:36.539
I am great.

00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:42.219
Vote for me R-Gen 1, the perfect president."

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:44.789
You can actually visualize it, can't you?

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:48.399
See for the longest time we've been so concerned
about robots taking over the world.

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:52.309
What most people don't realize is that it's
already happening.

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:54.030
We've become robots.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.640
Our educational system is structured to turn
us into followers.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.250
You see, what separates us from robots is
the fact that we have the ability to question

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.250
things.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.479
But we've stopped using that ability.

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:05.479
Think about it this way.

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:11.020
How is it that colleges are selling textbooks
for $200 to 18-year-old kids when it only

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.330
costs $6 to make?

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.220
Why is it that tuition costs as much as it
does?

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.710
And why is it that we're pressuring parents
to use their retirement savings to pay for

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.440
their kids' college education?

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.920
Does this make any sense to you?

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:29.780
This is why I believe this is the perfect
time for us to question our educational system

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:35.020
before it's too late.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:40.640
On January 24th Patrick Bet-David will launch
"Dropout and Get Schooled."

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:46.159
And you'll see how one book will disrupt the
entire educational system.

